[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Appendix A — the C build's optimisation level is part of the configuration
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so the documented build
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m command produces an unoptimised (`-O0`) reference library. That matters, because
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m GCC's choice of *destination operand* for the commutative `mulss`/`addss`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m instructions differs between `-O0` (no inlining, one instruction per C operator)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    111[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and `-O2` (everything inlined and operands re-canonicalised), and on x86 an SSE
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    112[0m:[38;5;10m[49m binary operation returns its destination operand when both operands are NaN. The
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m translation matches the `-O0` stream, which is what the specified build command
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m produces.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    115[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    116[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The blast radius of that choice was measured rather than assumed. Compiling the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    117[0m:[38;5;10m[49m unmodified `c_src/src/lib.c` at both `-O0` and `-O2` in a scratch directory and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    118[0m:[38;5;10m[49m comparing 5,000,000 uniformly random inputs through `dlopen`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    119[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    120[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    121[0m:[38;5;10m[49m n=5000000  -O0 vs -O2 differ=3649  of which ZERO-NaN-inputs=0
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    122[0m:[38;5;10m[49m n=5000000  -O0 vs -O2 differ=3649  of which NOT-pure-NaN-payload-differences=0
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    123[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    124[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    125[0m:[38;5;10m[49m So the two optimisation levels agree bit-for-bit on **every** input that contains
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    126[0m:[38;5;10m[49m no NaN, and all 3,649 divergences are differences in the payload/sign of a NaN
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    127[0m:[38;5;10m[49m *result*. The translation is therefore bit-identical to the C for the specified
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    128[0m:[38;5;10m[49m build at every input, and bit-identical to an `-O2` build at every NaN-free
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    129[0m:[38;5;10m[49m input.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    130[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
