[38;5;252m[1m## What was wrong[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The library is tiny — one exported function, [38;5;10mto_barycentric[0m, computing 2D barycentric coordinates — but the translation had a real bug. The prior Rust used per-operation [38;5;10masm![0m statements whose operand order was reverse-engineered from an [1moptimized[22m GCC build. [38;5;10mc_src/CMakeLists.txt[0m sets no [38;5;10mCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE[0m, so the reference library is [38;5;10m-O0[0m, where GCC doesn't inline [38;5;10mlm_dot2[0m and picks different destination operands. Since an x86 SSE binary op returns its [3mdestination[23m operand when both operands are NaN, several results diverged.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two fixes were needed:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
1. [1mCorrect operand order[22m, read off the actual [38;5;10m-O0[0m disassembly. Notably [38;5;10mlm_dot2[0m compiles with its [38;5;10my[0m product [3mand[23m its final [38;5;10maddss[0m operand-swapped relative to the C source text.[0m[0m
2. [1mA construction that survives LLVM.[22m Separate [38;5;10masm![0m statements were not enough — the operand order of a two-address inline-asm template is chosen by the register allocator, and it flipped for some [38;5;10maddss[0m/[38;5;10mmulss[0m steps depending on surrounding code. I replaced them with a single [38;5;10mglobal_asm![0m core ([38;5;10m.hidden[0m, so the export surface still matches) that transcribes the C instruction stream operation for operation.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Evidence[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- **Symbols:** [38;5;10mnm -D[0m diff is empty in both directions — no missing and no extra symbols. Enforced as a test, not a one-off command.[0m[0m
- **Phase B:** all 37 [38;5;10mCONFIGS.md[0m rows pass, spanning winding, degeneracy, scale regimes, every float class, and the reciprocal tail.[0m[0m
- **Phase C:** all 20 [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m rows pass. The C has [3mno[23m error channel (zero branches, zero pointers, zero enums — verified by grep against the header), so each row asserts an exact exceptional bit pattern rather than "both failed".[0m[0m
- **Fuzz:** 200,000,000 randomized differential cases, zero divergence.[0m[0m
- **Matrix:** the crate declares no features, so the single combination was run under [38;5;10m--no-default-features[0m, default, and [38;5;10m--all-features[0m × dev/release. No driver binary exists in either project.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two findings worth flagging:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m row 5 originally claimed a [38;5;10m-0.0[0m denominator. That is [1munreachable[22m — [38;5;10mdot00[0m, [38;5;10mdot11[0m and [38;5;10mdot01²[0m are all [38;5;10m≥ +0[0m. I corrected the row to the condition the C actually reaches: a [3mnegative[23m denominator from catastrophic cancellation, giving [38;5;10minvDenom = -inf[0m when it lands in the subnormal range. Confirmed by sweep (107,365 of 8M samples).[0m[0m
- Since "all tests green" is weak evidence on its own, I mutation-tested all 23 commutative instructions. 13 are observable and [1mall 13 were caught[22m. Of the 10 that weren't, 4 are literal squarings, and the remaining 6 were fuzzed 50M cases each and are genuinely indistinguishable from the C — [38;5;10mdot01[0m's and [38;5;10minvDenom[0m's NaN payloads are structurally masked by the subtractions they feed. Details in [38;5;10mCONFIGS.md[0m Appendix B.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
One caveat you should know about: bit-exactness for NaN inputs is tied to the C being built at [38;5;10m-O0[0m, which is what the documented CMake command produces. I measured the exposure — comparing [38;5;10m-O0[0m against [38;5;10m-O2[0m over 5M inputs, the two agree bit-for-bit on [1mevery NaN-free input[22m, and all 3,649 divergences are NaN payload/sign differences only. So if the reference is ever rebuilt with optimizations, only multi-NaN inputs could differ.[0m[0m
